","headline":"15…a4! The only good move here: every alternative is clearly worse.","points":["Attacks the bishop on b3.","Gains space: the pawn on a4 cramps White's pieces behind it.","The next best move, 15…Bxh3, would drop Black's winning chances from 85% to 55% (−0.53).","15…a4 wins a bishop for a pawn, picking it up with 16…axb3.","Sets up a sequence and wins a bishop for a pawn once the captures settle, picking it up with 16…axb3.","White answers 16.d5."]},{"ply":94,"name":"47…Nf5","cls":"mistake","color":"b","headline":"47…Nf5 is a mistake: Black's winning chances go from 94% to 80%.","points":["White answers 48.Qc5+, which gives check, so the reply is forced.","Better was 47…Qxf2 (−7.28), which takes the pawn on f2."],"better":"47…Qxf2 threatens …Qxg2#, with mate in 1, and wins a pawn. After 48.Qa7+ Kd6 49.Qb6+ Ke7 50.Qc5+ Ke6, Black comes out a pawn up (−7.28)."},{"ply":110,"name":"55…Ne6","cls":"blunder","color":"b","headline":"55…Ne6 is a blunder: Black's winning chances go from 83% to 50%.","points":["White answers 56.Qxd7+, which takes the bishop on d7.","The knight walks into a pin by the queen on d5.","After Qxd7+, White wins 3 points of material within 2 moves.","Better was 55…Ke8 (−4.22), which protects the bishop on d7, which was hanging."],"better":"55…Ke8 protects the bishop on d7. Engine line: 56.Qe4+ Kf8 57.Kg1 Ne8 58.f3 Qd6 (−4.22)."},{"ply":111,"name":"56.Qh5+","cls":"miss","color":"w","headline":"56.Qh5+ misses 56.Qxd7+, which wins material. White's winning chances go from 50% to 10%.","points":["Black answers 56…Kf8: the king steps out of check to f8.","After Kf8, Black wins 1 point of material within 4 moves.","Better was 56.Qxd7+ (+0.01), which takes the bishop on d7."],"better":"56.Qxd7+ wins a bishop. After 56…Kf8 57.Qc8+ Ke7 58.Qb7+ Kf8 59.Kg2, White comes out a piece up (+0.01)."},{"ply":124,"name":"62…Qe6","cls":"miss","color":"b","headline":"62…Qe6 lets the win slip: 62…Kf8 kept Black winning. Black's winning chances go from 84% to 51%.","points":["White answers 63.Qxe6+, which takes the queen on e6.","The queen walks into a pin by the queen on d5.","Better was 62…Kf8 (−4.48): the king steps out of check to f8."],"better":"62…Kf8 prepares …Ne7 and …Be8 and steps the king out of check to f8. Engine line: 63.g4 Ne7 64.Qd8+ Be8 65.f5 Qa1+ (−4.48)."},{"ply":125,"name":"63.Qf3","cls":"blunder","color":"w","headline":"63.Qf3 is a blunder: White's winning chances go from 49% to 13%.","points":["Black answers 63…Qe1+: the queen joins the attack: it now hits 3 squares around the White king.","Better was 63.Qxe6+ (−0.15), which takes the queen on e6."],"better":"63.Qxe6+ trades queens. After 63…Kxe6 64.g4 Ng7 65.f5+ Bxf5 66.gxf5+ Kxf5 67.Kh2, White comes out a pawn up (−0.15)."}],"opening":{"name":"Modern Defense","eco":"B06","points":["Both sides followed opening theory up to 8.Bc4: 15 moves in all, 8 by White and 7 by Black.","Theory runs out after 8.Bc4: too few games between strong players reached this position to go further."]}}